 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Verbs with fixed preposition",
   "texto": [
    "Some verbs are learned along with a preposition and their case: **warten auf + acusativo** (expect something / someone), **denken an + acusativo** (think about something / someone), **sprechen über + acusativo** (talk about something) and **sich interessieren für + acusativo** (interest in something). Example: **Ich warte auf den Bus** (I expect the bus).",
    "Not all the prepositions of these verbs are accusative: **sprechen mit + dativo** = talking to someone. Learn together the verb, the preposition and the case."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The Spanish trap",
   "texto": [
    "They are not translated word for word: in German «wait for» is **warten auf** and «pensar en» is **denken an**. We have to learn the preposition next to the verb.",
    "With «sich interessieren für», the pronoun changes: **Ich interessiere mich für Musik** (I'm interested in music). With «du» it would be **dich**."
   ]
  },
